  "title": "Local channel comparisons characterize unrestricted environment energy extrema, with a distinct fixed-charge repair",
  "topics": [
    "physics",
    "algebra",
    "optimization",
    "complexity",
    "acquisition",
    "methods"
  ],
  "claim_status": "source_derived_unreviewed",
  "reported_status": "Source-derived arguments and inspected producer replay; new extensions separately identified as integration-derived. Source and internally derived claims remain unreviewed. External correctness, historical priority and physical validity are UNKNOWN. Exact/floating diagnostics, producer-code replay and same-team analytic criticism do not independently validate universal mathematics, novelty or scientific capability.",
  "scientific_scope_status": "Supplied finite h0,h1 on active A and collar C; arbitrary finite R and common Hermitian K on CR, containing no changed active terms. Source unrestricted ground-energy endpoint characterization is separately extended to nonnegative integer charges at fixed Q using strongly charge-preserving channels and a graded universal environment class. No practical electronic-structure advantage or realistic-environment convergence theorem.",
